  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Water-Meter Register",
    "overview": "A counter is a utility meter read at a glance. Countsy sets every value as a row of black drum tiles with light digits on a cool enamel-grey ground, under a single meter-blue plate. The system is flat, outlined and instrumental: nothing is decorated, and every surface exists to make the number legible first.\n\nDensity is phone-first and calm. One card per counter, one number per card, a full-width minus and plus pair beneath. Dark mode is an instrument panel, not a recolor: the ground drops to near-black and the drum tiles invert to light tiles with dark digits.",
